  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Solving a linear inequality requiring a sign reversal</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Solve the following inequality for \(x\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle {@a@} - {@b@}x > {@c@} \)
</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as an inequality. Use <b>&lt;</b> for less than and <b>&gt;</b> for greater than. For example, <code>x < 5</code>)</i></p>
<p>Equation: [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>
<p>To solve the inequality, we need to isolate \(x\).</p>

<p>First, we group the constant terms on the right side by subtracting \({@a@}\) from both sides.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \begin{aligned}
-{@b@}x &> {@c@} - ({@a@}) \\
-{@b@}x &> {@c - a@}
\end{aligned} \)
</p>

<p>Next, we divide both sides by \(-{@b@}\).</p>
<p><i><b>Crucial Rule:</b> Because we are dividing by a negative number, we must <b>reverse</b> the inequality sign.</i></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \begin{aligned}
x &< \frac{{@c - a@}}{-{@b@}} \\
x &< {@x_val@}
\end{aligned} \)
</p>

<p>Hence, the correct solution for this inequality is:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \boxed{x < {@x_val@}} \)
</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
